# Density Compare
# Silver (Ag) — real density 10.49 g/cm³. equal masses: Silver vs water — sides ∝ (1/ρ)^(1/3).
scene "Silver Density Compare"

element_cube = cube 9.1mm material: silver at (-20mm, 4.6mm, 0)
water_cube = cube 20mm material: water at (18mm, 10mm, 0)
# both cubes weigh the same: about 83.7 g — the water cube is the reference
